<%
const toc = [
  ['quick-answers', 'Quick answers'],
  ['mission', 'Our mission'],
  ['who-we-serve', 'Explore your path'],
  ['about-tabs', "Who it's for"],
  ['how-it-works', 'How it works'],
  ['commitment', 'Our commitment'],
  ['faq', 'FAQ'],
];
%>
<header class="page-head about-head">
  <div class="container page-head__inner">
    <div>
      <ol class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">About us</li></ol>
      <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
      <h1>About Youth Futures Canada — careers in Canada for young talent everywhere</h1>
      <p class="lead">Youth Futures Canada is a Canadian job bank built for young people building a career here — students, graduates, young professionals and skilled workers, in Canada or exploring it from anywhere in the world — and for the employers and third-party consultants who hire them. Our promise is in our name: <strong>our dreams, our skills, our future, our Canada.</strong></p>
    </div>
    <div class="page-head__actions">
      <a class="kds-btn kds-btn--accent" href="/employer">Post a job — <%= price.employer.base %>/month + GST</a>
      <a class="kds-btn kds-btn--brand" href="/jobs">Browse jobs across Canada</a>
      <a class="kds-btn kds-btn--ghost" href="/jobseeker">Join free as a job seeker</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="about-stats-band">
  <ul class="about-stats container" aria-label="Youth Futures Canada at a glance">
    <li><strong><%= price.employer.base %></strong><span>+ GST, per employer posting monthly</span></li>
    <li><strong><%= price.consultant.base %></strong><span>+ GST, per consultant posting monthly</span></li>
    <li><strong>5</strong><span>career stages, one Job Bank</span></li>
    <li><strong>13</strong><span>provinces &amp; territories</span></li>
    <li><strong><%= C.CATEGORIES.length %></strong><span>job categories</span></li>
    <li><strong>Free</strong><span>for every job seeker</span></li>
  </ul>
</div>

<nav class="about-jump" aria-label="Jump to section">
  <ul class="container about-jump__list">
    <% toc.forEach(([id, label]) => { %><li><a href="#<%= id %>"><%= label %></a></li><% }) %>
  </ul>
</nav>

<div class="about-main">
  <%- include('_quick', { quick }) %>

  <section class="about-section about-quote" id="mission" aria-labelledby="mission-h">
    <div class="container about-quote__inner">
      <div class="about-quote__lede-col">
        <p class="about-quote__mark" aria-hidden="true">“</p>
        <h2 id="mission-h" class="about-quote__lede">Real Canadian opportunities for young talent, wherever you're starting from.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose about-quote__text">
        <p>Most job boards assume you already live where the job is. Youth Futures Canada was created for young people building a career in Canada from any starting point — students and graduates looking for a first role, young professionals ready to take their skills further, skilled workers with a trade or technical background, and newcomers, Indigenous job seekers and refugees among them. We are a <strong>Canadian job bank</strong>, not an immigration consultancy: every listing is a real opportunity from a real Canadian employer, presented honestly.</p>
        <p>We keep the model simple on purpose. Employers and third-party consultants pay one flat, published price per posting — <%= price.employer.base %> + GST for employers, <%= price.consultant.base %> + GST for consultants posting on behalf of clients. Job seekers never pay anything. Every listing is searchable by category, province, city, job type and work arrangement, and every job seeker can tell us who they are so that the right opportunities find them. No hidden fees, no bidding for visibility, no pay-to-apply.</p>
        <p>Our name says exactly what we do: <strong>Youth Futures Canada</strong> connects young talent everywhere with careers in Canada, from Toronto and Vancouver to the smallest community in Nunavut.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <%- include('_audiences', { cities }) %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="audience-tabs-h">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="audience-tabs-h" class="visually-hidden">Who Youth Futures Canada is for</h2>
      <div class="about-tabs" id="about-tabs">
        <input type="radio" name="about-audience" id="tab-employers" class="about-tabs__input" checked>
        <input type="radio" name="about-audience" id="tab-consultants" class="about-tabs__input">
        <input type="radio" name="about-audience" id="tab-seekers" class="about-tabs__input">
        <div class="about-tabs__nav" role="tablist">
          <label for="tab-employers">For employers</label>
          <label for="tab-consultants">For consultants</label>
          <label for="tab-seekers">For job seekers</label>
        </div>
        <div class="about-tabs__body">
        <div class="about-tabs__panels">
          <section class="about-tabs__panel about-tabs__panel--employers prose" aria-labelledby="employers-h">
            <h3 id="employers-h">Hiring in Canada shouldn't take a sales call</h3>
            <p>Youth Futures Canada works for employers at any scale — a restaurant in Halifax, a trucking outfit in Winnipeg, a hospital network in Ontario, a software team in Vancouver — all looking to bring in students, graduates, early-career hires and skilled young professionals. Set up your company once, then post whatever you need, whenever you need it.</p>
            <h4>One rate, published, no negotiating</h4>
            <p><strong><%= price.employer.base %> CAD</strong> per posting per month, plus 5% GST (<%= price.employer.gst %>) — <strong><%= price.employer.total %> CAD</strong> total. Every business pays the same amount in every province, that rate holds for as long as the posting runs, and each payment lands a numbered receipt in your Billing tab, ready to download whenever your books need it.</p>
            <h4>What has to be on a posting</h4>
            <p>Youth Futures Canada mirrors the fields job seekers already expect from a Canadian job bank: a real work location (not just a city — street, unit, postal code, and every site if there's more than one), the name your business actually goes by up front with the registered legal name underneath, pay and its schedule, an education/experience bar pulled from standard lists, an industry tag and an optional NOC code. Candidates can print the whole thing to one page.</p>
            <h4>Renewal happens automatically, cancellation doesn't wait</h4>
            <p>A posting keeps renewing month to month so it never vanishes from search mid-cycle without warning. Pull it whenever you want from your dashboard — let it run out the paid month or drop it immediately, whichever you'd rather. No contract locks you in either way.</p>
            <h4>Once a posting stops running</h4>
            <p>A lapsed payment, a manual cancel, or you pausing it — any of the three archives the job. Archived listings disappear from search, alerts, the sitemap and their own page, so nobody applies to something that's already closed. Everything about it, applicants included, stays in your dashboard, and a couple of clicks brings the same posting back to life if you need it again.</p>
            <p><a href="/employer">Read the full employer guide and pricing →</a></p>
          </section>
          <section class="about-tabs__panel about-tabs__panel--consultants prose" aria-labelledby="consultants-h">
            <h3 id="consultants-h">Third-party consultants and recruiters</h3>
            <p>Staffing agencies, immigration consultants placing newcomers, HR firms hiring for clients — anyone posting on someone else's behalf runs it through a Third Party Consultant account, which holds one profile per client and lets you manage every one of them, and every applicant, from a single login.</p>
            <p>The consultant rate is <strong><%= price.consultant.base %> CAD</strong> per posting per month plus 5% GST (<%= price.consultant.gst %>), <strong><%= price.consultant.total %></strong> total — set per posting, dropped whenever you're done with it. Candidates see the client's own name on every listing, never your agency's. One Billing screen holds every client's subscriptions and receipts, each ready to download as a PDF.</p>
            <p><a href="/consultant">See how consultant accounts work →</a></p>
          </section>
          <section class="about-tabs__panel about-tabs__panel--seekers prose" aria-labelledby="seekers-h">
            <h3 id="seekers-h">Free, always</h3>
            <p>Looking for work in Canada shouldn't cost you a cent here, and it never will. Set up a profile in a few minutes, drop in your resume as a PDF or Word file, and from there every application, saved job and status update lives in one dashboard you can check any time.</p>
            <p>Tell it what you're after — categories, province and city, on-site or remote, experience level, the communities you identify with — and matching roles land in your inbox as soon as they go live, either right away or bundled into a daily digest, whichever you'd rather. Nobody but the employer or consultant behind a job you actually apply to ever sees your resume.</p>
            <p><a href="/jobseeker">Create your free job seeker profile →</a></p>
          </section>
        </div>
        <aside class="about-tabs__aside">
          <div class="about-tabs__aside-card">
            <p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
            <dl>
              <div><dt>Employers</dt><dd><%= price.employer.base %> + GST /month</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Consultants</dt><dd><%= price.consultant.base %> + GST /month</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Job seekers</dt><dd>Free, always</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="kds-btn kds-btn--accent kds-btn--block" href="/employer">Post a job</a>
            <a class="kds-btn kds-btn--ghost kds-btn--block" href="/jobseeker">Create a free profile</a>
          </div>
        </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section about-flow" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-h">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Two ways in</p>
        <h2 id="how-h">How Youth Futures Canada works</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-flow__grid">
        <div class="about-flow__panel">
          <div class="about-flow__head">Post a job</div>
          <ol class="about-steps__list">
            <li><strong>Set up your profile.</strong> One company profile for employers; consultants add a separate one per client they represent.</li>
            <li><strong>Put the role together.</strong> Title, description, category, where it's actually based (list more than one site if needed), the job type, pay and period, and who you're hoping to reach.</li>
            <li><strong>Pay and it's live.</strong> <%= price.employer.base %> + GST as an employer, <%= price.consultant.base %> + GST as a consultant. The posting appears right away, matching candidates get pinged, and it keeps renewing monthly until you cancel it.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="about-flow__panel about-flow__panel--alt">
          <div class="about-flow__head">Find a job</div>
          <ol class="about-steps__list">
            <li><strong>Sign up free.</strong> Create your profile and upload your resume (PDF, DOC or DOCX).</li>
            <li><strong>Search or wait for alerts.</strong> Filter jobs by province, city, category and work arrangement, or let matched alerts come to you.</li>
            <li><strong>Apply online.</strong> One click sends your resume to the employer. Track the status of every application from your dashboard.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section about-commit-section" id="commitment" aria-labelledby="commit-h">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our commitment</p>
        <h2 id="commit-h">What we hold ourselves to</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="about-commit-grid">
        <li class="about-commit-tile about-commit-tile--a"><span class="about-commit-tile__n">01</span><h3>Inclusion</h3><p>Youth Futures Canada serves young people at every career stage. Every posting can also be tagged for the communities it explicitly welcomes, and job seekers can search by that too.</p></li>
        <li class="about-commit-tile about-commit-tile--b"><span class="about-commit-tile__n">02</span><h3>Accessibility</h3><p>We build with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) in mind: semantic structure, keyboard navigation, visible focus, labelled forms and readable contrast on every screen size.</p></li>
        <li class="about-commit-tile about-commit-tile--c"><span class="about-commit-tile__n">03</span><h3>Privacy (PIPEDA)</h3><p>Personal information is handled in line with Canada's Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act. We collect only what the job bank needs, and resumes are never exposed by public link.</p></li>
        <li class="about-commit-tile about-commit-tile--d"><span class="about-commit-tile__n">04</span><h3>Canadian data</h3><p>Youth Futures Canada is a Canadian service for the Canadian labour market: prices in Canadian dollars, GST handled correctly, and your data kept on infrastructure we control.</p></li>
      </ul>
      <aside class="about-cite">
        <h3>How to cite us</h3>
        <p>When referencing this page, please cite it as: <q>Youth Futures Canada, “About Youth Futures Canada — careers in Canada for young talent everywhere,” <%= canonical %>.</q></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <%- include('_faq', { faq }) %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="close-h">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cta-band">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Get started</p>
        <h2 id="close-h">Your future starts with the right opportunity.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Whether you're hiring in Calgary, recruiting for clients across Quebec, or looking for your first job in Canada from anywhere in the world, Youth Futures Canada is ready for you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-band__actions">
        <a class="kds-btn kds-btn--brand" href="/employer">Post a job — <%= price.employer.base %> + GST</a>
        <a class="kds-btn kds-btn--brand" href="/jobseeker">Sign up free</a>
        <a class="kds-btn kds-btn--ghost" href="/contact">Contact us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
